hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11056","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Affan, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: Habib bin Abi Amra told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of God Almighty: “Whatever land you cut down or leave standing on its roots, it is by God’s leave.” And to disgrace the transgressors. He said: They will be sent down from their fortresses. They were ordered to cut down the palm trees. Their hearts were moved, so the Muslims said: It is true. We cut some of it and left some of it, so let us ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there any reward for us for what we cut off, and do we have to pay for what we left off? And a burden? Then God Almighty revealed: “Whatever soft tree you cut or leave standing.” He said: Affan narrated this hadith to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid, on the authority of Habib, then he came back and we told him on the authority of Hafs (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11057","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, who was Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn The two events are that Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: I will inform you of this loss. Indeed, God Almighty singled out His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with something that he did not He would give him someone else, and he said: And whatever God has given to His Messenger of them, you have not given him horses or riders to pay, so these are for the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace in particular. By God, he did not choose it over you, nor did he prefer it over you. He divided it among you until this portion of it remained. Money, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to spend from it on his family for their year, and then put what was left in the money of God Almighty.” Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11058","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id, Yahya ibn Musa, and Harun ibn Abdullah informed us, and they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, on the authority of Umar ibn al-Khattab, “The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was from what God gave to His Messenger, from what he did not repay.” The Muslims were on it, with horses and riders, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to spend a year’s worth of it on his family, and whatever remained he put it in Weapons and spears are equipment for the sake of God.”"
"11059","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Hurmuz. He said: Najda wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about things. I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read his letter, and when he wrote to him, “Indeed, You asked about the share of relatives that God mentioned. Who are they? And we see that the kinship of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is us. Our people refused that to us"
"11060","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Mansour bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, And Ibn Abbas, that they bore witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “forbade: the dabba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the tampered earth.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it."
"11061","Muhammad bin Rafi’ and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Adam, he said: Al-Mufaddal bin Muhalhal told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “May God curse: tattooed women, tattooed women, and tattooed women, And those who reveal the beautiful, those who change God’s creation.” Then a woman from Banu Asad, called the mother of Jacob, reached the news, and she came to him and said: He informed me. That you cursed Kate and Kate? He said: Shall I not curse whoever curses the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while it is in the Book of God? She said: I have read what is between the Qur’an, and what have I found? He said: If you had read it, you would have found it. Did you not find: And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it? She said: Yes, and I think your family does some of that. So he said: Go in and see. So she entered and then left. She said: I did not see anything. He said: If you had done it, you would not have intercourse with us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11062","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Mubashir bin Abdullah told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, On the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Mecca, and that Abu Bakr and Omar, and the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were among the emigrants, because they abandoned the polytheists, and among the Ansar were emigrants, because Medina was a home. Shirk, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Aqaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11063","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Maimun, saying: He advised Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and said: “I advise the caliph after me to fear God, and I advise him to treat the first emigrants: who They were expelled from their homes, the sign is that their migration would be known to them, and their virtue would be known to them, and I command the Ansar: and those who sought refuge. abode and faith from before them the sign, that their virtue should be known to them, and that it should be accepted from their doers of good, and that he should overlook their wrongdoers, and I advise him The people of the protection of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he fulfill his covenant with them, not burden them beyond their capacity, and fight Their enemy is behind them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11064","Hannad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man, from the Ansar A guest spent the night with him, and he had nothing but food for his children. So he said to his wife: Put the girl to sleep, put out the lamp, and offer something to the guest. You have, so it was revealed: And they prefer themselves, even if they are poor."
"11065","Abdah bin Abdullah informed us, he said: Husayn, meaning Ibn Ali al-Jufi’i, informed us, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Once, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zuhair bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of indecency, for God does not like indecency and indecency, and beware of stinginess. For He destroyed those who were before you. He commanded them to commit injustice, and they were unjust. He commanded them to commit immorality, so they committed immorality. He commanded them to sever ties, and they were sundered."
"11066","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We used to recite the tashahhud during prayer. So we say: Peace be upon God before His servants, peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael, we enumerate the angels, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God is peace, so when one of you sits in prayer, let him say: Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and His mercy.” God and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, so if One of you said: “Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. It has befallen every righteous servant in heaven and earth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11067","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I memorized it on the authority of Amr. H And Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told me, he said: Ubayd Allah told me Ibn Abi Rafi’, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, informed him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me, Al-Miqdad, and Al-Zubayr. So he said: “Go until you come to the Khakh Garden, for there is a woman there with a letter, so take from her.” So we set off until we came to the Khakh Garden. So, behold, we were in distress, so we said: Bring out the letter. So she took it out from her punishment, and behold, in it was: From Hatib bin Abi Balta’ah to Some people from the people of Mecca were telling them about some matter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: What is this, Hatib?” He said: “Do not be hasty on me, O Messenger of God, for I was a person attached to the Quraysh, and I was not one of them.” Those who are with you have relatives through which they protect their kinship, so I loved, since I missed that lineage, to draw near to them by the hand they protect. She is my kin, and I did not do it out of disbelief or apostasy from my religion, nor did I consent to disbelief after Islam. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have He told you the truth.” Omar said: O Messenger of God, let me behead him, meaning this one. He said: “O Omar, and how do you know? Perhaps God has seen the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you.” And the wording is for the servants of God. Muhammad added in his hadith: Then God Almighty revealed: Do not take my enemy and your enemy as the entire Surah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11068","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, he said: Ibn Shihab, he said: and he told me Urwa bin Al-Zubair, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the believing women migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings be upon him, will be tested by the words of God Almighty: O Prophet, when the verse comes to you of believing women. Aisha said: Whoever acknowledges this? Believing women, he acknowledged the ordeal, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, acknowledged that, he said to them, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Go, for I have pledged allegiance to you.” No, by God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never touched a woman, except that he He pledged his allegiance to them verbally. Aisha said: By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never took anything from women, except by what God commanded him, and it was He says when he takes over them, he says: “I have pledged allegiance to you,” words (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11069","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: When this was revealed The verse: “When the believing women come to you, pledging their pledge of allegiance to you,” he said: “And he will not disobey you in what is right.” She said: “There was some wailing from him,” and I said: “Except the family of so-and-so.” Because they had made me happy during pre-Islamic times, I must make them happy. He said: “Except the family of so-and-so.”"
"11070","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a gathering, and he said: “You pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you do not associate anything with God, and you do not steal, and you do not commit adultery.” He read The verse is upon them, so whoever of you fulfills his duty, his reward is with God, and whoever of you is afflicted with any of that, God will cover it for him, it belongs to God, if He wills. He tortured him, and if he wished, he would forgive him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11071","Al-Harith bin Miskin said, I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Ruqeeqa said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some women to pledge allegiance to him on Islam, so I said: O Messenger of God, come. We pledge allegiance to you on the condition that we will not associate anything with God, nor will we steal, nor commit adultery, nor bring any slander that we invent between our hands and our feet, nor We disobey you in what is right. He said: “In what you are able and able to do.” So we said: God and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. Come, we will pledge our allegiance to you, O. Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not shake hands with women, but my words to a hundred women are the same as my words to one woman.” Or like I said to one woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11072","Ali bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of Maan bin Issa, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have five names: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, and I am Al-Gatherer at whose feet people will be gathered. “I am the Eraser through whom God erases disbelief, and I am the One who punishes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11073","I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala. He said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “When God Almighty wanted to raise Jesus, peace be upon him, to heaven, he went out to his companions while they were in a house, twelve men, and his head was Dripping water, he said: Which of you will my likeness be cast upon and he will be killed in my place and be with me in my rank? Then a young man of the youngest of them stood up and said: Me. He said: Sit, then he repeated it to them, so the young man got up and said: I, so he said: Sit, then he repeated it to them the third time, so the young man said: I, so he said: Jesus, peace be upon him: Yes, you are. So the likeness of Jesus, peace be upon him, was cast over him. Then Jesus was raised from a platform that was in the house to heaven, and he came. The request was from the Jews, so they took the young man due to his similarity, killed him, then crucified him, so they separated into three groups, and one group said: God Almighty was among us. As He willed, then He ascended to heaven, and these are the Jacobites, and a group said: The Son of God was among us as God willed, then God raised him to Himself. These are the Nestorians, and a group said: The servant of God and His Messenger was among us as long as God willed, then he took it away. These are the Muslims, so they demonstrated. The two infidel women attacked the Muslim woman and killed her, and Islam remained obliterated, until God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God Almighty revealed: So a group of the Children of Israel believed and another group disbelieved, meaning the group that disbelieved in the time of Jesus, peace be upon him, and the group that believed in At the time of Jesus, we supported those who believed over their enemy by making Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, prevail over their religion over the religion of the disbelievers, so they became victorious. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11074","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We were sitting With the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when Surat Al-Jumu’ah was revealed. When he recited: And others of them, as they joined them, he said: Who are these people? Messenger of God? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not check with him until he asked him once, twice, or three times. He said: And among us is Salman al-Farisi. He said: So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, put May God bless him and grant him peace, then he said: “If faith were with the Pleiades, men from these people would have attained it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11075","Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abtar told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Friday, when a caravan carrying food passed by, and it came out.” people to twelve men, then the verse of Friday was revealed.”"
"11076","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Arqam, he said: “When Abdullah Ibn Abi said what he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, so I told him, and he swore that he did not say it, and the people started saying: Are you telling a lie to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I sat at home for fear that if people saw me they would say: You lied, until God Almighty revealed this verse: When the hypocrites come to you, they say: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of God, the sign"
"11077","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Wasil al-Ahdab, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: It was said to him: Are there more hypocrites today or during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Rather, today they are more, because at that time they kept it secret, but today they make it known.”"
"11078","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he told me Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, said: We were sitting in a group in which there was Abdullah, and Hudhayfah came until he stood over us, so he greeted us and then said: It has been revealed. God cursed hypocrisy against a people, and they were better than you. Al-Aswad said: Glory be to God. Indeed, God Almighty says: Indeed, the hypocrites are in the lowest level of Fire, so Abdullah smiled, and Hudhayfah left, until he sat at the side of the mosque, and Abdullah got up, and his companions dispersed, he said: Fermani With pebbles, so I went to him, and Hudhayfah said: I was amazed at his laughter, and he knew what I said. Yes, God Almighty has sent down goodness upon a people. of you, then they repented, so God turned to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11079","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, and Ibn Abi Adiy told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka'b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Battle of Tabuk, and Abdullah bin Ubayy said: If we return to Medina, they will expel from it the more honorable and the meaner. So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and Abdullah swore He did not mention anything, and my people blamed me and said: Why did you do this? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to me and said: “Indeed, God Almighty has revealed your excuse, so this verse was revealed: Those who say no Spend on those who are with the Messenger of God until they disperse, until it has reached: If we return to Medina, they will surely expel from it the more honorable and the meaner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11080","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, meaning Ibn Muhammad bin Ayan, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, that he heard Zayd ibn Arqam said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey during which the people were afflicted with distress. Abdullah ibn Ubayy said, “I Listen to his companions: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of God until they disperse from around him. And he said: If we return to Medina, they will be expelled. The more honorable is the humbler. He said: So I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him that. He sent for Abdullah bin Ubayy and asked him, So he made an effort to take his right hand. They said: Zayd, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lied. So I felt distress from what they said, until God Almighty sent down My belief in: When the hypocrites come to you, he said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called them to ask forgiveness for them, so they turned their heads. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11081","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Invaders, so a man from the immigrants kicked a man from the Ansar, and the immigrants said: Oh the immigrants, and the Ansari said: Oh the Ansar, so he heard it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “What is the matter with the claim of pre-Islamic times?” They said: O Messenger of God, a man from among the immigrants knelt upon a man from the pre-Islamic era. The Ansar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave her, for she is stinking.” This reached Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul, and he said: Did they do it? ! If we return to Medina, they will expel from it the more honorable and the meaner. Then Omar said: Let me behead this man, said the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “People do not tell us that Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, kills his companions.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11082","Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim informed us, he said: Malik informed us, on the authority of al-Fudayl ibn Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Niyar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out before Badr, and when he was in Harrat al-Wabara A man who was remembered for his courage and help overtook him. The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rejoiced when they saw him. When they overtook him, He said: O Muhammad, I have come to follow you and travel with you? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you believe in God and His Messenger?” He said: No. He said: “Go back, for we will not seek help from a polytheist.” Then he went on, until when we were in the tree he overtook him, and he said to him as he said the first time, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him as he said The first time, he said: No, he said: “Go back, for I will not seek help from a polytheist.” So he came back, then he caught up with him in the desert, and he said to him as he said the first time, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you believe in God and His Messenger?” He said: Yes, he said: “So go.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11083","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Abu Al-Zubayr informed me That Ibn Umar said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: “O Prophet, if you divorce women, divorce them before their waiting period.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11084","I am Ahmad bin Nasih, I am Ismail, I am Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, on the authority of Mujahid, Ibn Abbas said: God Blessed said And God Almighty: “O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them before their waiting period.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11085","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Al-Mu`tamir. He said: I heard him speaking in a whisper, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: He made the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace This verse, peace be upon him: And whoever fears God, He will make a way out for him, until he concluded the verse, then he said: “O Abu Dharr, if all people They took it, it was enough for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11086","I am Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, our name is Al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Muhammad bin Ayan. He said: Zuhair, our Abu Ishaq, told us on the authority of the lions, Masruq, and Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, “Sura An-Nisa al-Qasra was revealed after Al-Baqarah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11087","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, we are Amr bin Aoun, I am a partner, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, that Ibn Masoud said, “ Al-Qasra was revealed after Surah Al-Baqarah: “And those who are pregnant, their term is that they should give birth to their burden.”"
"11088","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’, we are told by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zurai’, Hajjaj, who is the Sufi, told us, we are told by Yahya bin Abi Kathir, we are Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said: It was said to Ibn Abbas, regarding a woman who gave birth twenty nights after the death of her husband: Is it appropriate for her to Do you get married? He said: “No, except the last of the two terms.” He said: I said: God, Blessed and Most High, said: “And pregnant women whose term is to give birth to their burden.” He said: “It is only This is about divorce. Abu Hurairah said: I am with my nephew, meaning Abu Salamah. So he sent his servant Kurayb and said: Go to Umm Salamah and ask her: Was this a Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he came to him and said: She said: Yes, Sabayah al-Islamiyyah was placed after his death. He married her off for twenty nights, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to get married, and Abu Al-Sanabel was among those who proposed to her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11089","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad told me, my father, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He had a female slave whom he had intercourse with, but Aisha and Hafsa did not stay with him until he made her unlawful. Then God Almighty revealed: O Prophet, why have you made unlawful what May God make it permissible for you if you seek ills, until the end of the verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11090","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he heard Ubaid bin Umair, he said: I heard Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. You claim that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to stay with Zainab and drink honey from her, so you and Hafsa joined each other, O Una Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her, she should say: I smell a sweet scent from you. So he entered upon one of them, and she said that to him, and he said: Rather, I drank honey at Zainab’s house,” and he said to me: “I will not go back to him.” So it was revealed: Why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you? If you repent to God, and when The Prophet confided something to some of his wives, saying: “Rather, I drank honey,” all in the hadith of Ata’. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11091","Abdullah bin Abdul-Samad bin Ali told me, on the authority of Mukhlid, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “A man came to him and said: ‘I have made my wife forbidden to me?’ He said: ‘You lied. She is not forbidden to you.’ Then he recited this verse: ‘O Prophet, why “You forbid what God has made lawful for you. You are required to do the most severe of expiations: freeing a slave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11092","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. Malik said: Abu al-Nadr told me, on the authority of Ali bin Husayn, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that: He asked Omar: About the two women who rebelled against the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Aisha and Hafsa. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11093","I am Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hushaym, I am Hamid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered Peace be upon him and his wives were jealous of him, so I said: Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you, will give him wives better than you, so I descended like that."
"11094","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: I told my father Usama: I am telling you about Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abbas al-Jashmi, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, a surah in the Qur’an of thirty verses intercedes for its companion until he is forgiven, blessed be He.” In whose hand is the kingdom.” Abu Usama acknowledged it and said: Yes."
"11095","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: I heard Mujahid speaking, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by May God bless him and grant him peace upon two graves, and he said: “They will be tormented, but they will not be tormented for a grave. As for this man, he was not concealed from his urine. This man was going around gossiping, then he called for a fresh bunch of grass, split it in two, and planted one on this one, and on that one, then he said: “Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they do not become dehydrated.”"
"11096","I am Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhayfah, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No one who kills himself will enter Paradise.”"
"11097","I am Muhammad Ibn Al-Muthanna, I am Muhammad, I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Ma’abad Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Haritha Ibn Wahb, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Shall I not direct you to the people of Paradise? Every one is weak and vulnerable. If he swore an oath to God, he would fulfill it.” And he said: “The people of Hell are all willing to accept it.” “arrogant arrogant man” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11098","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, from Ubayd Allah, from Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: That is a loincloth. He said: A man from Quraysh who had a loincloth like the loincloth of a sheep."
"11099","I am Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Bishr, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “I was victorious with youth, and Aad was destroyed with the hornet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11100","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he says. And I am Yusuf bin Isa, I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, I am Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever’s account is discussed will perish.” I said: O Messenger of God, for God says: Who? And Joseph said: As for him who has been given His book is in his right hand {7} Then he will be given an easy reckoning {8} He said: “That is the reward.”"
"11101","I am Al-Abbas bin Muhammad, I am Yunus, I am Nafi’ bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever is held accountable on that day will be punished.” She said: O Messenger of God, an easy reckoning? He said: “That is the accident, and whoever discusses the account will perish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11102","I am Bishr bin Khalid, narrated to us by Abu Usama, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “A questioner was asked about a punishment that will befall him. He said: Al-Nadr bin Al-Harith bin Kalada.”"
"11103","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Muhammad bin Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Suhail narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no man who does not pay the zakat on his wealth but on the Day of Resurrection, a fire will be made of fire, and his forehead will be burned with it.” And his forehead, and his back, in a day whose equivalent is fifty thousand years, until it is judged among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11104","I am Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-A’mash. I am Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus, on the authority of Abtar, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Tamim ibn Tarfa, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon us while we were separated, and he said: Why do I see you so defenseless? \. The pronunciation is by Hannad (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11105","Ahmad bin Mani’ told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Zakaria, then he mentioned a word that means “I am David”, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: We said To Abdullah: Did any of you accompany the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of the jinn? He said: None of us accompanied him except me. We spent a night in Bishr where some people spent the night. We missed him, so we said: He was taken away or assassinated. So we dispersed through the paths and valleys, looking for him. I met him coming from the direction of Hira, and I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for the night we spent the night there. My people, and he said: “Indeed, the caller of the jinn has come to me, so I responded to them by reciting to them the Qur’an,” and he showed me their traces, and the traces of their fire. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11106","I am Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, we are Abu Al-Walid, we are Abu Awanah. And I am Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Muhammad bin Mahboub, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out with a group of his companions, heading to the market of Ukaz, and he was separated between the devils and the news of heaven.” And meteors were sent upon them, and the devils returned to their people, and they said: There is a barrier between us and the sky. And meteors were sent upon us, and he said: What Nothing has happened between you and the news of the sky, so look to the easts and wests of the earth and see what this is that has come between you and the news. The sky? So they set out to attack the easts and wests of the earth, seeking what had come between them and the news of the sky. Then those people departed. The group who headed towards Tihama went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was at Nakhlah, heading to the market of Okaz, while he was praying. led his companions to the dawn prayer, and when they heard the Qur’an, they listened to it and said: This is God who has come between you and the news of heaven. There is a time They returned to their people and said: O our people, we have heard a wondrous Qur’an {1} that guides to right path, so we believe in it, and we will never associate anything with our Lord. Uhud {2}, so God revealed: “Say, ‘It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened, but it was revealed to him only the words of the jinn.’” The pronunciation is for Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11107","I am Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif, we are Abu Al-Walid, we are Abu Awanah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, neither read anything about the jinn nor saw them.”"
"11108","I am Abu Dawud, we are Ubaidullah, I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The jinn were ascending To heaven, they listen to the revelation, and when they hear the word, they add to it nine times. As for the word, it is truth, and as for what they add, it is Falsely, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, they were prevented from taking their seats, so they mentioned that to Satan, and the stars had not been targeted at them before. Then Satan said to them: This is nothing but something that happened on earth. So he sent his soldiers, and they found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing. He was praying, so they came to him and told him, and he said: This is the event that happened on earth.”"
"11109","I am Ismail bin Masoud, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, from Sa’id, from Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said We went to Aisha, asked her permission, and we entered. I said: Tell me about the rise of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Didn’t you You recite this Surah: O Almighty One? I said: Yes, she said: “For God assumed the standing at the beginning of this Surah, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions stood for a year, until Their feet swelled, and God withheld its end for twelve months, then God Almighty sent down the mitigation at the end of this Surah, so it became “The voluntary night prayer after an obligatory prayer.” Summary (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11110","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Yazid, meaning bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, and he said after him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She told him that whenever she got into trouble, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say to her: “O daughter of Abu Bakr.” Then Qutiba mentioned A word that means “girdle your waist.” He used to spend as much of the night as God willed until he stood up for his prayers, and he rarely slept at night when he said God Almighty said to him: “Stand up all night, except for a short time.”"
"11111","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Muhammad bin Ja’far, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, he said: I heard Ya’qub bin Asim bin Urwa bin Masoud, and Abdullah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God said: “The Antichrist will emerge, and God Almighty will send Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon him, as if he were Urwa bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi, so he seeks him and destroys him, then the people will remain after him for nine years, with no enmity between the two, then God will send Glory be to Him, may He be glorified and exalted, a cold wind from the Levant, so do not leave anyone with an atom’s weight of faith in his heart without taking it away, even if one of you was in like the top of a mountain you entered upon them.” He said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “And the worst of people remain in the fear of birds and dreams. The wild beasts do not know what is right, nor do they reject what is wrong, so Satan appears to them and commands them to turn to idols and worship them, while they are in That is the basis of their livelihood, their good livelihood. Then the trumpet will be blown and no one will be left except that they will be shocked. Then God will send or God will send down rain. Then the bodies of the people will sprout from it, then another will be blown into it, and behold, they stand and watch. Then it will be said: O people, come to your Lord. Stop them, they will be responsible. Then he said: Bring out the people of Hell. It is said: How much? It is said: Out of every thousand, nine hundred and nine. And ninety days, and on that day the children will be raised with gray hair, and on that day a shin will be uncovered.” Muhammad bin Ja’far said: Shu’bah told me this hadith, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, and I showed it to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11112","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar, on the authority of Al-Mu’affa, who is Ibn Imran, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Hazm, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, in his saying: “They are the people of piety and the people of forgiveness,” he said: Your Lord says: “I am worthy to fear that a god other than me will be appointed with me, and whoever fears that a god other than me will be appointed with me, then I am worthy to forgive him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11113","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, narrated by Hujain bin Al-Muthanna, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I heard Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, saying: Jabir bin Abdullah told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Then the revelation waned from me for a while, while I As I was walking, I heard a voice between the heavens and the earth, so I looked up towards the heavens, and behold, the angel who had come to me in Hira was sitting on a throne between the heavens and the earth. So I came in groups until I fell to the ground, then I came to my family and said: Hug me, Hug me, and they gathered me together, then God Almighty revealed: O you! Al-Muddathathir { 1 } Arise and warn { 2 } And your Lord, so magnify { 3 } And purify your clothes { 4 } And disgrace, so abandon { 5 } Abu Salamah said: Disgrace Idols, then the revelation became heated and continued.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11114","Mahmoud bin Khalid, na Omar, told me on the authority of Al-Awza’i. He said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: I asked Abu Salamah: What is the Qur’an? It came down before? He said: O Muddaththir, I said: Or read in the name of your Lord who created? He said: I asked Jabir bin Abdullah: Which Qur’an was revealed before? O Muddaththir, I said: Or read in the name of your Lord who created? Jabir said: Shall I not tell you about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I lived near Hira for a month, and when I had spent my time, I went down and explored the depths of the valley. I was called and looked. In front of me and behind me, and to my right and left, but I did not see anything. Then I was called and I looked in front of me and behind me, but I did not see anything. Then I was called and I looked in front of me and behind me. And to my right and to my left, but I did not see anything. Then I looked at the sky, and behold, He was on the throne in the air. A trembling overcame me, so I came. Khadija, so I commanded them and they covered me, so God Almighty revealed: O you who cover up {1} arise and warn {2} and your Lord, so magnify {3} And purify your clothes {4}.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shayban disagreed with him."
"11115","I am Al-Rabi’ bin Muhammad bin Issa, from Adam, from Shayban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz narrated to me. Al-Zuhri, that Jabir bin Abdullah told him: The first thing revealed from the Qur’an: O Muddathathir, Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “I was surrounded by Hira, and when I had finished my neighbourhood, I went into the depths of the valley. Then a caller called out, so I looked to my right and to my left.” And behind me, I did not see anything, so I looked above me, and I saw Gabriel sitting on a throne between the heavens and the earth, so I came from him, and came to Khadija, so I said: Cover me, cover me, so they covered me, and they poured cold water on me, and he said: O you who cover me up. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11116","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Abu Awanah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “No Move your tongue with it to hasten it. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was suffering from a severe revelation. He used to move his lips. Ibn Abbas: I will move them for you as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to move them. Saeed said: I will move them as Ibn Abbas used to move them. He moved them, so he moved his lips, so God Almighty revealed: Do not move your tongue with it to hasten with it. {16} Indeed, it is upon Us to collect it and recite it. {17} He said: Collect it in your chest, then we recite it. So when we recite it, follow his recitation. He said: So listen and be silent. So he was the Messenger of God. When Gabriel came to him, may God bless him and grant him peace, he listened, and when Gabriel departed, he recited it as he had recited it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11117","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, we are Ubaid Allah bin Musa, I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his saying: “Do not move your tongue with him to hasten him.” He said: He was moving his tongue for fear that it would escape him."
"11118","I am Ahmad bin Abdah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Saeed, who is Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When the Qur’an is revealed to him, he hastened to recite it in order to memorize it. Then God Almighty revealed: Do not move your tongue with it, to His saying: And His Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11119","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, we are Muhammad, meaning Ibn Thawr, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The people said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Are you harmed by the sun when there are no clouds below it?” They said: No. He said: “Are you harmed by the moon on the night when there is no full moon?” Below it are clouds.” They said: “No, O Messenger of God.” He said: “You will see it like that on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11120","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Abu Al-Numan, Abu Awanah told me. And I am Abu Dawud, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: I told Ibn Abbas: “Is it better for you? So is it better? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it, and God Almighty sent it down? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it. God bless him and grant him peace, then God sent it down.” The word is for Abraham (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11121","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am a partner, on the authority of Al-Makhul bin Rashid, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: The revelation of the prostration, and whether it came upon a person. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11122","I am Muhammad Ibn Rafi’, I am Abd al-Razzaq, I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, in his saying: Zamharir, Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman said, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The fire complained to its Lord, and said: My Lord, some of me have devoured others, and He has consumed me. So he gave her permission every year for two breaths. He said: “The harshest cold you will find is the hot water of Hell, and the harshest heat you will find is the heat.” Hell (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11123","I am Muhammad bin Salamah, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik. And Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, Malik told me, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Umm al-Fadl heard him reciting: And the mursalat according to custom, so she said: O my son, you reminded me of your reciting this surah. It is the last thing I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting it in Morocco.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11124","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman bin Abdul Malik, from Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a cave, and this was revealed to him: And the mursalat by custom, so we We will surely catch it from its mouth when a snake came out to us, so we went ahead of it and it entered its hole. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It was protected from “Your evil is as you have been protected from its evil.” Al-Amash added in his hadith: Abdullah said: We will receive fresh water from his mouth. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Hafs bin Ghayath disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Al-A’mash L3629, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad."
"11125","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in fear of Mina, until she descended, as is customary, and a serpent came out, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Kill her.” So we ran to her, and she entered her hole."
"11126","I am Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, I am Abdullah bin Wahb, we are Al-Layth. And I am Wahb bin Bayan, we are Ibn Wahb, we are Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “None of you should say: the vineyard, for the vineyard is only the Muslim man’s, but say: the grape gardens.” The pronunciation is Yunus, and Wahb is like it."
"11127","I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, narrated by Mu’mal bin Al-Fadl, narrated by Issa, on the authority of Ismail, narrated by Tariq bin Shihab: that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was still It is mentioned about the Hour, until it was revealed: They ask you about the Hour, when will it arrive, the entire verse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11128","I am Abu Al-Ash'ath Ahmad ibn Al-Miqdam, Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, told us, Shu'bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, On the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The one who is skilled in the Qur’an is with the honorable and righteous traveler, and the one who He suffers in it, and it is difficult for him, so he has two rewards.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11129","I am Abu Dawud, narrated by Arim, narrated to us by Thabit bin Yazid, narrated to us by Hilal bin Khabab, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “You will be gathered barefoot and naked.” He said: Then his wife said: Should we look or see each other’s private parts? He said: O so-and-so, every one of them will have a matter on that day that will enrich him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11130","Amr bin Uthman told me, na Baqiya, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” Then Aisha said to him: O Messenger of God, so how? With private parts? He said: “Every one of them will have a matter on that day that will enrich him.”"
"11131","I am Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, we are Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal, we are Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman, we are Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Alqamah bin Qais, On the authority of Salama bin Yazid al-Jafi, he said: My brother and I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, In pre-Islamic times, our mother used to honor guests and maintain family ties. Did that work benefit her in any way? He said: “No.” He said: “So she had a sister of hers in pre-Islamic times, but she had not yet reached the age of perjury?” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The woman who is married and the woman who loves the woman will be in Hell, unless the woman who loves the woman realizes Islam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11132","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, we are Muhammad, we are Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, he said: “I prayed behind The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the morning, and I heard him reciting: “I do not swear by the unclean” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11133","I am Yusuf bin Isa, I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, I am Mas’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid, who is Ibn Sari’, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, who said: “I prayed behind the Prophet. He prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, the dawn prayer, so I heard him reciting: “By the night when it is dark.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11134","I am Muhammad ibn Qudamah, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Muadh got up and prayed the afterlife, but it was long. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So, O Muadh, where were you during: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High’, ‘Dhuha’, ‘and when the sky opened up?’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11135","I am Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr. Abu al-Nadr Hashim bin al-Qasim, narrated to me by Ubayd Allah al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ubaid Al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Anas, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed and said: “Do you know Why did you laugh? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Of a servant addressing his Lord, saying: O Lord, have you not saved me from injustice? He says: Yes, he said: Then he says: I do not take it against myself except with a witness from me. Then he says: Your own self is sufficient as a witness over you today, and the honorable. The writers are witnesses, then a seal is placed in it, and its corners are said: Speak of its actions. Then a break is made between it and the words, and it is said: After you. And damn, I used to struggle with you.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith on the authority of Sufyan other than Al-Ashja’i, and it is a strange hadith, and God knows best."
"11136","I am Muhammad bin Aqeel, alias Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When the Prophet God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the city. They were among the most wicked people in their measure, so God Almighty revealed: “Woe to those who exaggerate.” So they measured well after that. \that\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11137","I am Suwayd bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Bahz bin Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Woe to the one who speaks and lies in order to make the people laugh. Woe to him, woe to him.”"
"11138","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I am Abu Dawud, Ya’qub told us, my father told me, on the authority of Salih, Nafi’, that Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the day when people to the Lord of the Worlds, on the Day of Resurrection, until one of them disappears to half his ears in his nostrils on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ubayd Allah did not mention: “On the Day of Resurrection.” Ubayd Allah said: “Until he rises,” and Abu Dawud said: “Until he disappears.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11139","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his saying: “On the day when people will rise up to the Lord of the Worlds,” he said, “One of them will stand up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11140","From Qutayba bin Saeed, from Al-Layth, from Ibn Ajlan, from Al-Qaqa’, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If a servant commits a sin, a black spot is struck in his heart. His heart, and if he increases it again until it rises to his heart, then he is the one who mentioned to God: No, rather, what they were earning was seen in their hearts."
"11141","I am Ziyad Ibn Ayyub, I am Ibn Ulayya, I am Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Whoever is held accountable on the Day of Resurrection will be punished.” She said: I said: God Almighty said: He will certainly be held accountable with an easy reckoning. He said: “Not that.” By the reckoning, that is only the present. Whoever is discussed with the reckoning on the Day of Resurrection will be punished.”"
"11142","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah read “With them: When the sky split open, he prostrated in it. When he left, he told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in it.”"
"11143","I am Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān, narrated to us ʿAffān ibn Muslim, narrated to us Ḥammād ibn Salamah, narrated to us Thābit al-Bunānī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Ṣuhayb, that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said:\n\n\There was a king among those who came before you"
"11144","I am Amr bin Ali, I am Abdul Rahman, narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite At noon and afternoon: when the sky splits open, and by the sky and al-Tariq, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11145","I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb, I am Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, In his saying: “And a witness and one who is witnessed. He said: The witness is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what will be witnessed on the Day of Resurrection, and that is his saying: So how? “When We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11146","I am Amr bin Mansour, narrated by Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Muadh prayed the Maghrib prayer, so he recited: Al-Baqarah, and women. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So, O Muadh, it was not enough for you to recite with: by the heaven and by the Tariq, by: And the sun in the morning hours? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11147","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, from Abu Awanah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan Ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite on the two Eids and on Friday: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and has He come to you? The hadith of Al-Ghashiya, and perhaps they gathered together in one day, and he recited them both.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11148","I am Ismail bin Masoud, neither Khaled, nor Shu’bah. He said: I am Abu Ishaq. He said: I heard Al-Bara’. He said: He was the first to come to us. The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Musab bin Umair and Ibn Umm Maktum, then Ammar, Saad, and Bilal came to us, then came Othman in the twenty, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and we did not see the people of Medina rejoicing over anything as happy as they were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. So he did not proceed until the verse was revealed: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,” and a surah from Al-Mufassal. Othman"
"11149","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, narrated by Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Muadh bin Jabal Al-Ansari led his companions for the evening prayer, and it was long. Then one of us left and prayed, and Muadh was told about him, and he said: He is a hypocrite. When that news reached the man, he entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He told him what Mu’adh had said, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Do you want to be a seducer, O Mu’adh, when you lead people? So recite with: the sun in its bright morning, and glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and recite in the name of your Lord, and by the night when it covers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11150","I am Zakaria bin Yahya, I am Nasr bin Ali, I am Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When it was revealed: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,’ he said: It is all in the scriptures of Abraham and Moses. He said: “It is fulfilled that no bearer of burdens should bear the burden of another.”"
"11151","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that Al-Dahhak bin Qais asked Al-Nu’man bin Bashir: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite on Friday following Surah Jumu’ah? He said: “He was reciting: Has the hadith about cheating ever reached you?”"
"11152","I am Amr bin Mansour, narrated by Abu Nu’aym, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was ordered That I fight people until they say: There is no god but God. If they say: There is no god but God, then their blood and their property are protected from me, except with due rights. And their reckoning is with God.” Then, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he recited: “You are only a Reminder {21} and you are not in control over them. {22}"
"11153","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, from Zayd bin Hubab, Ayyash bin Uqba told me, Khair bin Nu’aym said, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And the dawn {1} and the ten nights {2}, he said: the tenth of the sacrifice, and the Witr on the day of Arafat, and the intercession \Day of Sacrifice\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11154","I am Abdah bin Abdullah, I am Zaid and he is Ibn Hubab, we are Ayyash, Khair bin Nu’aym told me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, the Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “And the dawn {1} and the ten nights {2}. He said: The tenth of Adha, the odd-numbered prayer on the day of Arafat, and the shaf’ on the day of sacrifice. \""
11155"""
"11155","I am 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam; Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, from Sulayman, from Muharib ibn Dithar, they both said: from Jabir, who said: Mu'adh led a prayer, and a man came and prayed with him. Mu'adh prolonged the prayer, so the man prayed in a corner of the mosque, then left. This reached Mu'adh, and he said: ""A hypocrite."" This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he asked the young man. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I came to pray with him, but he prolonged it for me, so I left and prayed in a corner of the mosque, then I tended to my camel."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Mu'adh: ""Are you a cause of trial (fitnah), O Mu'adh? Why did you not recite: 'Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High' (Surah al-A'la), 'By the sun and its brightness' (Surah al-Shams), 'By the dawn' (Surah al-Fajr), and 'By the night when it covers' (Surah al-Layl)?"""
"11156","I am Amr bin Zurarah, I am Ismail, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Muadh bin Jabal used to lead his people in prayer. So Haram entered and wanted to water his palm trees, so he entered the mosque to pray with the people. When he saw Mu’adh, he continued for a long time in his prayer, and he caught up. With his palm trees to irrigate them, he said: He is a hypocrite, he hastens to pray for the sake of a palm tree. Then Haram came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while Muadh was with him, and he said: O Prophet of God, I wanted to water my palm trees, so I entered the mosque. To pray with the people. When Mu’adh took a long time, I moved forward in my prayer and joined my palm trees to water them. He claimed that I was a hypocrite, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came He, peace be upon him, greeted Muadh, and he said: “Are you a tempter? Do not dwell on them. Read with: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High’, and the sun and its brightness, and the like.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11157","I am Muhammad bin Rafi’, and Harun bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zama’a, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentions the she-camel that he slaughtered. He said: “When the most wretched of hers was sent forth, and he said: A powerful, mighty, mighty, invincible man was sent for her.” Rahatah, like Abu Zam’a.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11158","I am Ahmad bin Sulaiman, from Miskin bin Bukayr, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: “We came to the Levant, So I entered the Damascus Mosque and asked Abu Darda’, and he said: How can Abdullah recite: “And the night when it covers, and the day when it appears, the night and the remembrance.” And the female 0? He said: This is how Abdullah used to recite it. Abu Darda said: I heard it like this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11159","This is Ali bin Hajar, this is Ismail, on the authority of Dawud. And I am Al-Hasan bin Qazah. I am Maslamah bin Alqamah, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amir, that Alqamah bin Qais said: I came to the Levant and met Abu Al-Darda', and he said: Where are you from? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: From which of them? I said: From the people of Kufa. He said: So you recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd? I said: Yes, he said: “Recite to me: And the night when it covers, and I recited to him: 0 And the night when it covers, and the day when it appears, and the Remembrance And the female 0, he said: I heard it like this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And the pronunciation is good"
"11160","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Al-Mu`tamir, he said: I heard Mansour speaking, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, said: We were at a funeral in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was attending in Baqi al-Gharqad, and he came The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sat down and had a piece of paper with him. He lowered his head and mocked it, then raised his head and said: “None of you “There is not a single soul that has been destroyed except that God has recorded its place in Paradise and Hell, whether it has been written as miserable or happy.” Then a man from the people said: Oh Messenger of God, shall we not abide by our letter and abandon work, so whoever is among the people of happiness will be happy, and whoever is among the people of Misery to lead to misery? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, work, for every person is facilitated. As for the people of happiness, happiness is facilitated, and as for the people of misery, so they facilitate misery.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: As for he who gives and fears {5} and is truthful. With the good {6} We will make it easy for the hardship {7} And as for him who is miserly and becomes self-sufficient {8} and denies the good {9} We will make it easy for the hardship {10}.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11161","I am Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was attending a funeral: “There is not one of you who does not have his seat marked from Hell and his place is in Paradise. They said: O Messenger of God, shall we not rely? He said: “Work, for every person will be facilitated. So as for him who gives and fears {5} and believes in goodness {6} - We will make it easy for ease {7} and as for him who is miserly.” And he became self-sufficient {8} and denied the good {9} So We will make it easy for hardship {10}.”"
"11162","It is narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar, it is narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, he said: It was said: O Messenger God, do you know the people of Paradise from Hell? He said: “Yes.” He said: What do the workers do? He said: “Everyone is facilitated for what he was created for.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11163","I am Ismail bin Masoud, from Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, from Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Jundub, who said: “Gabriel delayed On the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a woman from the Quraysh said: His owner has left him, so it was revealed: And the forenoon {1} and the night When he sat down {2}”"
"11164","I am Qutaybah bin Saeed. Al-Layth, who is Ibn Saeed, narrated to us. I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, who said: “I prayed with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had dinner, and he recited: “With figs and olives.” Malik said: Al-Atama"
"11165","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, narrated by Al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, narrated by Nuaym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu said Ignorance: Did Muhammad cover his face among the polytheists? It was said: Yes. He said: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, if I saw him like that, I would trample on his neck, or I would rub his face in the dirt. Then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said the salaam while he was praying, then stepped on his neck. He said: He did not surprise them except that he was turning on his heels and guarding himself with his hand. It was said: What is the matter with you? He said: Between me and him is a ditch of fire, terror, and wings! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he had come close to me, the angels would have snatched him up, limb by limb.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11166","I am Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Khalid, who is Suleiman bin Hayyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Then Abu Jahl came and said: Did I not forbid you from doing this? By God, you know what there is in it more than I do. Then God Almighty revealed: “Let him leave his caller {17} We will leave the female slave {18}.” Ibn Abbas said: By God, if he had called his caller, she would have taken him. Zabaniyah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11167","I am Muhammad ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdul Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in his statement: Glory be to Him. God Almighty said: “We will leave the immoral woman.” He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Abu Jahl had done so, the angels would have caught him with their own eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11168","I am Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, and he said: “Seek it in the last seven nights of the month of Ramadan.”"
"11169","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, from Khalid, from Shu’bah. He said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying as he bowed: “Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11170","I am Ismail bin Masoud, from Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Kahms, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I told the Prophet, “Pray May God bless him and grant him peace: If Laylat al-Qadr falls, what should I say? He said, “You say: O God, you are pardoning and love to pardon, so pardon me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11171","I am Muhammad bin Qudamah, I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, his saying: “We sent it down on the night of Destiny, he said: The Qur’an was revealed as one sentence on the Night of Destiny, and God Almighty used to reveal part of it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the wake of some, they said: “If the Qur’an had not been sent down to him in one sentence, then We would certainly have strengthened your heart thereby, and We would have recited it as a hymn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11172","I am Muhammad bin Bashar, we are Abdul Rahman, we are Jabir bin Yazid bin Rifa’ah Al-Ijli, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh He said: “If it were not for your foolish people, I would have put my hand in my ears and called out: Indeed, the Night of Decree is the twenty-seventh night.” He who did not lie to me informed about News from the one who did not tell me a liar, meaning on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Your foolishness has fallen. A letter from my book (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11173","I am Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan, from Hajjaj, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ubayy bin Ka`b when it was revealed: “It is not those who disbelieve: Indeed, God has commanded me to recite to you: It is not those who disbelieve.” He said: And he named me for you? He said: “Yes,” and he cried"
"11174","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I am Ziyad bin Ayyub, Muhammad bin Al-Ala’, and Al-Hasan bin Ismail. They said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Al-Mukhtar bin Falful. He mentions, he said: I heard Anas, he said: A man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: O best of creation, he said: “That is Abraham,” and Abu Kurayb said. And Al-Hasan belongs to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ziyad said: He mentions on the authority of Anas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11175","I am Suwaid bin Nasr, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read this verse: “On that day its news will be told.” He said: “Do you know what its news is?” He said: They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Its news is that it will bear witness against every male and female slave of what was done on its back. She says she did such-and-such on such-and-such day.” He said: “These are her reports.”"
"11176","I am Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad, from my father, from Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I heard Al-Hasan, saying: from Sa’sa’ah, the uncle of Al-Farazdaq, who said: “I came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I heard him say: “So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it {7} and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it {8} He said: I don’t care if I don’t hear anything else, that’s enough for me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11177","I am Ahmad bin Musrif bin Amr, we are Zayd bin Hubab, we are Shaddad bin Saeed, we are Ghailan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Creating has distracted you, until it ended it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11178","I am Muhammad bin Amr, we are Yahya bin Saeed, we are Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Procreation has distracted you {1} to the point that you visited graves {2}. He said: The son of Adam says: My wealth is my wealth, and what you have of your wealth is what you eat. “So you wore it out, or you put it on and it did not work out, or you gave it and you went on.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11179","I am Muhammad bin Yahya Abu Ali, from Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is by the One in whose hand is my soul, the bliss about which you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection: cold, wet and cool shade, with cold water on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11180","I am Nuh bin Habib, we are Abdul-Malik bin Hisham Al-Dhimari, we are Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he recited: “He thinks that his wealth has given him eternal life.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11181","I am Amr bin Ali, we are Amer bin Ibrahim, and he was trustworthy and one of the best people, we are Khattab bin Jaafar bin Abi Al-Mughirah, he said: My father told me, On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the words of God Almighty: “For Ilaf,” he said: “My blessing upon the Quraysh,”: for Ilaf them during the winter journey. And in the summer, he said: They used to spend the winter in Mecca, and summer in Taif, so let them worship the Lord of this House {3} who fed them from hunger. And secure them from fear {4}"
"11182","I am Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun, on the authority of Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ubi, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears, God will hear him, and whoever sees, God will see.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11183","I am Qutaybah bin Saeed, from Abu Awanah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “Every good deed is charity. We used to count supplies as The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was devoid of fullness and destiny.”"
"11184","I am Ali bin Hajar, I am Ali bin Mushar, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, One day, we appeared in the mosque, when he fell asleep, then raised his head smiling, and I said to him: What made you laugh, O Messenger of God? He said: “A surah has just been revealed to me. In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar. {1} So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. {2} It is your choice. It is the most severe {3} Then he said: Do you know what Al-Kawthar is? We said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “It is a river and my Lord has promised me Paradise.” Blessed and Most High, His vessels are greater than the number of the stars. They will return them to my nation, and the servant will be shaken by them, and I will say: O Lord, he is one of the My nation, and he says: You do not know what happened after you.”"
"11185","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib, Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdul-Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, What is Kawthar? He said: “A river that my Lord gave me in Paradise. It is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. In it are birds whose necks are like the necks of carrots.” Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of God, it is soft. He said: “The one who eats it is softer than it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11186","I am Muhammad bin Kamil, I am Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Bishr, and Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said in Al-Kawthar, he said: “It is the great goodness that God, Blessed and Most High, has given him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11187","I am Ahmad bin Harb, from Asbat, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: I said to Aisha: What is Al-Kawthar? She said: “A river given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the interior of Paradise.” I said: What is the interior of Paradise? She said: “In the middle, both edges are a hollow circle.”"
"11188","I am Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Ubaida, on the authority of Humaid Al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas bin Malik. And I am Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Yazid bin Zuray’, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I entered Paradise.” Then I saw a river rimmed with pearls, so I plunged my hand into its stream, and when it stopped, I exclaimed, I said: O Gabriel, what is this? “This is the Kawthar that God has given you.”"
"11189","I am Amr Ibn Ali, I am Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “When Ka’b Ibn Al-Ashraf came to Mecca, The Quraysh said to him: You are the best of the people of Medina and their master. He said: Yes. They said: Don’t you see this person who is estranged from his people? He is better than us, and we mean: the people of the Hajj and the people of Sadana. He said: You are better than him, so it was revealed: Indeed, your case is the amputee. And it was revealed: Have you not seen those who were given a share of the Scripture who believe in the oppressive force and the tyrant, to His saying: You will not find a helper for him."
"11190","I am Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim, narrated by Marwan, narrated by Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he recited in the two rak’ahs of Fajr salutations: “Say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is Allah, the One.’”"
"11191","I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, Yahya, meaning Ibn Adam, told us, Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then the coming of you has not brought you.” I said: I have come, O Messenger of God, to teach me something that I should say. When I was sleeping, he said: “When you go to bed, recite: Say, O you disbelievers, then sleep at the end of it, for it is a release from polytheism.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11192","I am Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he often says in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to You, O God, our Lord, and with Your praise, O God, forgive me.” He interprets The Qur’an"
"11193","I am Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar He used to ask the immigrants about this verse: When God’s victory and conquest come, what was it revealed about? Some of them said: God commanded His Prophet, when he saw people entering Islam and striving in the religion, to thank God and seek His forgiveness. He said Omar: Don’t you like Ibn Abbas? O Ibn Abbas, come on, why don't you speak? He said: He asked him when he would die. He said: “When God’s victory and conquest {1} come and you see people entering God’s religion in droves {2}, then this is your sign from “Death.” He said: “You have spoken the truth, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I did not know of it, except what you knew.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11194","I am Amr bin Mansour, we are Muhammad bin Mahboub, we are Abu Awanah, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When it was revealed: When God’s victory and conquest come, until the end of the surah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mourned when it was revealed. So he began to exert himself as hard as he could regarding the matter of the Hereafter, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said after that: “The conquest has come, and the victory has come.” By God, and the people of Yemen came.” A man said: O Messenger of God, and who are the people of Yemen? He said: “A people whose hearts are gentle, whose hearts are soft. Faith is Yemen, wisdom is Yemen, and jurisprudence is Yemen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11195","I am Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, narrated by Jaafar, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays. And I am Ahmad bin Suleiman, from Jaafar bin Aoun, from Abu Umays, from Abdul Majeed bin Suhail, from Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: O Ibn Utbah, do you know the last surah of the Qur’an that was revealed? I said: Yes, when God’s victory and conquest come, he said: You have spoken the truth.” The wording is by Ahmad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11196","I am Hanad bin Al-Sirri, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash. And I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala, from Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He ascended The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at Safa one day, and he said: “O morning,” and the Quraysh gathered to him, and they said: What is the matter with you? He said: “What if I told you that the enemy was coming to you in the morning or in the evening, would you not believe me?” They said: Yes. He said: “For I am a warner.” “For you are at the hands of a severe torment.” Abu Lahab said: This is why you have called us all, so God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: May Abu Lahab’s hands repent. To the end (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11197","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid bin Hunayn, said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: I arrived with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He heard a man reciting: “Say, ‘He is God, the One.’” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It has become obligatory.” I said: “What has become obligatory?” He said: “Paradise.”"
"11198","Abdul Rahman bin Khalid told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Malik bin Mughal told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of His father, that he entered the mosque with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and saw a man praying, saying: Oh God, I ask you that I I bear witness that there is no god but You, the One and Only, the Eternal, the One who did not give birth and was not born, and there is no one equal to Him. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, he has asked Him by His greatest name, by which He gives, when asked, and responds when called upon.”"
"11199","On the authority of Qutaibah, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Asim, and Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, both of them on the authority of Zirr, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Ka’b, about The two exorcists, and he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “I was told, so I said,” so we say as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said hello"
"11200","On the authority of Harun bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever forgets a prayer or forgets to perform it, its expiation is for him to pray it when he remembers it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11201","On the authority of Abu Al-Tahir bin Al-Sarh, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, both on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd Al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Sa’id and Abu Hurairah: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw dirt in the qibla of the mosque, so he scratched it off. With a pebble, then he forbade a man to spit to his right, or in front of him, but to spit to his left, or under his left foot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11202","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Ulaqah al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “I pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May peace and blessings be upon him for advising every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11203","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa bin Yunus bin Abi Ishaq al-Subai’i, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “It is obligatory The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Zakat al-Fitr to young and old, male and female, free and slave: a saa’ of dates, or A saa’ of barley,” and on the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, with it, and on the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, with it."
"11204","On the authority of Humayd ibn Masada, on the authority of Yazid ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Kulayb Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let those of you who are forgiving and forbidding be gentle, then those next to them. Then those who follow them, and do not differ lest your hearts differ, and beware of the distractions of the markets.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11205","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Azhar bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar struck a land In Khaybar, he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to consult him about that, and he said: “If you wish, you can retain its originals and give it in charity.” So he retained Its origin is that it should not be sold, given away, or inherited, so it should be given in charity to the poor, relatives, slaves, the needy, and the wayfarer. As for the guest, there is no sin on the one who is its guardian if he eats from it in a reasonable manner, or feeds his friend without being greedy for it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11206","On the authority of Harun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Maan bin Issa, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: A man broke his fast during Ramadan, during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he ordered him to make expiation by freeing a slave, or fasting for two months, or Feeding sixty poor people. He said: He said: I do not find it. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a sweat of dates, and he said: “Take this and give it in charity,” and he said: O Messenger of God, I do not find anyone more in need of it than I am. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his fangs showed, then he said: “Eat it.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11207","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Ghandar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whichever woman is married to a guardian, it belongs to the first of them, and whoever sells something from two men, it belongs to the first of them.”"
"11208","On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair Al-Yazani, Marthad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most deserving of conditions is that you fulfill what You have made private parts lawful with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11209","On the authority of Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Sa’dan bin Yahya, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and my camel became tired, so I wanted to leave it alone. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed me and prayed for him. And he struck him, and he walked a path that he had never walked before. He said: “Sell him for a small amount of money.” I said: No. He said: “Sell him for a small amount of money.” So I sold him for a small amount of money. I withdrew his lambs to Medina, so when we reached Medina, I brought him the camel and paid its price. Then I returned, and he sent for me and said: “Do you think I only chased you to take your camel? Take your camels and your dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11210","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two parties trade at option as long as they do not separate. If they tell the truth and explain it, they will be blessed in their sale, but if they lie and conceal it, the blessing of their sale will be valid.”"
"11211","On the authority of Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “For every sale there is no sale between them until they separate, except for the sale of options.” On the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad Al-Harrani, on the authority of Mukhlid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, with it. On the authority of Qutaibah, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, that Abdullah bin Dinar had it. On the authority of Amr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Bahz ibn Asad, on the authority of Shu`bah ibn al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, with it. On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ishaq bin Bakr bin Mudar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Had, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11212","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abdul Ala, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The sale is at option unless they separate, or one of them says to the other: Choose,” and on the authority of Ziyad ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Ismail ibn Aliya, on the authority of Ayoub, with it. On the authority of Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. On the authority of Qutaibah, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, both on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11213","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahik, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me.” And it is safe to sell what I do not have.” On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ishaq Al-Marwazi, on the authority of Khaled bin Khadash, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ayyub, with it. Hammad said, Ayyub narrated it to me. On the authority of Humayd bin Masada, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Ayoub, with it. On the authority of Imran bin Yazid, on the authority of Marwan al-Fazari, on the authority of Awf and another mention - both of them, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11214","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, and Humayd bin Masada, both of them, on the authority of Yazid bin Zurai’, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to advance or sell, nor are there any conditions in a sale, nor is it permissible to sell what you do not have.” On the authority of Ziyad bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, with it. On the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hussein al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, with it. On the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, with it. On the authority of Harun bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Matar Al-Warraq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, With it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11215","On the authority of Ibn Muthanna, on the authority of Abbad, the author of the Karabis, on the authority of Abdul Majeed, he said: Al-Adadah ibn Khalid said to me: Shall I not read to you a letter he wrote for me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I said: Yes, so he brought out a letter for me: “This is what Al-Adadah bin Khalid bin Hawdha bought from Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He bought it from him.” A male or female slave who is neither sick, nor predatory, nor evil, a Muslim is sold by a Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11216","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Dawud, on the authority of Amr ibn Aoun, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Musa ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Grasshopper, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man has more right to his property if he finds it, and the sale shall be followed by the one who sold it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11217","On the authority of Ziyad bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He forbade: muqāṭāliḥah, muzabānah, mukhtābārah, and from the second, unless it is known.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11218","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, and Muhammad bin Rafi’, both on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave, his money belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, And whoever sells a palm tree containing fruit that has ripened, its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.” The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11219","On the authority of Muhammad bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever sells a palm tree that contains fruit that has sprouts, then its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates it.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Mattar bin Tahman is weak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11220","On the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Mu’id Hafs bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar. On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave while he has money, he gets his money, unless he stipulates The buyer, and whoever plants a palm tree and sells it after planting it, gets its fruit, unless the buyer stipulates.” And on the authority of Ahmed bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. On the authority of Ahmad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Musa, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Abi Mulaika, they said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: . . . So he mentioned it as a messenger (Peace Be Upon Him)"
